      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Case 20-444, United States versus Gary. Mr. Ellis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. Ellis, under the government's theory, does it matter which element a district court omits during the plea colloquy, or does the omission of an element never constitute structural error?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JEFFREY L. FISHER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. Fisher, I -- I want to talk just a moment about your unanimous -- you know, the proposed futility exception. What -- what does it take to satisfy that? Unanimous view of the circuits but only three circuits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our rule would do nothing more than return an average of one Section 922 case to each district judge, as the government's own statistics demonstrate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Is -- is -- is your Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: That is my argument today, Justice Kagan, because that is the nature of the error. I mean, I think what you just said is very much what the Court said in the Faretta line of cases, which is no matter how ridiculous it was for the defendant to represent himself or no matter how guilty he may have been, if we violated that right as a -- as a court system, the defendant gets automatic relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-20-444",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "07f7e570cbfa14bfb4a4e070b3604476bc922e5ebf6d4324634c7bec10f686d4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-07f7e570cbfa-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: I -- I don't deny there was sufficient notice, but that was never the test the court applied. The case I would most readily direct you to is the Hormel decision at 341."
    },
    {
